the uncharted franchise is about many  things but secrets and treasure might be  at the top of that list luckily mr drake  and i go way back and he trusts me with  all his secrets in this video we're  talking about a handful of things you  may not know about the uncharted  franchise for more dude raider content  make sure to subscribe to gamespot  for starters let's talk about the man  that initially inspired nathan drake's  personality and no i'm not talking about  indiana jones even though he did play a  major factor in it as well i'm talking  about johnny knoxville of jackass fame  during a 2015 interview with the verge  naughty dog's josh sheer revealed early  in development there was a version of  nate with a comically emotive face that  was partially based on knoxville the  idea was later scrapped and the team  decided to go the more traditional  handsome lead character out and johnny  if you're watching this they said it not  me you're gorgeous and speaking of  gorgeous men did you know harrison ford  starred in an uncharted commercial if  not that's totally understandable as  they only aired in japan to promote the  release of uncharted 3. in the video  ford can be seen playing the game's  iconic airplane and chateau chapters  while whispering jump and grab it as if  nate can actually hear him something  we're probably all guilty of the whole  thing feels like watching your favorite  grandpa play your ps3 on thanksgiving  the action just keeps on coming  i think it's very  which are very uh  realistic and and  very dramatic  but come on you've gotta admit it's  pretty cool to see indiana jones in  uncharted's world meet for a brief  period  i wonder if harrison ford plans on  seeing the uncharted movie a movie that  once had mark wahlberg as the nathan  drake roll what no this casting took  place in around 2009-2010  when the movie was first trying to get  the ball rolling on production  unfortunately the film changed writers  and directors more than new jersey  changes weather i swear one day i'm  freezing and the next did forget it back  to uncharted eventually marky mark  dropped off the project and the role was  offered to everyone's favorite italian  plumber chris pratt fortunately pratt  turned the role down and even though  nathan fillion expressed interest in his  role as drake in the fan film was  fantastic the role was ultimately given  to peter parker himself in 2017 some  fans thought that phillium was too old  to play drake but now fans believe that  tom is too young to play him hey how old  is jake anyway well i'm glad you asked  devante both amy hennig the game's  writer and nolan north the voice of  drake have revealed in interviews that  nathan is 31 in uncharted one using some  clues from dialogue and assuming the  character's age in real time with each  game release that would make our hero 33  and uncharted 2 35 and uncharted 3 and  the big 4-0 in uc-4 and by the end of  uncharted 4 when we meet cassie who is  around 10 to 14 years old we can assume  nate has crossed into his 50s and is  officially too old for this [ __ ] but  speaking of cassie did you know that she  was named after nate's mother aka her  grandmother cassandra morgan that's  right nate's last name is morgan and  drake is the last name he and brother  sam chose for themselves to honor  cassandra's theory that francis drake  had heirs  you ready for this  hell yeah  and here's one more name fact for you  the drake morgan family dog is named  vicki after victor sullivan and while  some people might feel disrespected to  have a dog named after them sully  actually gave nathan okay during the  hidden and plain sight chapter of  uncharted 4. and speaking of being  hidden in plain sight let's talk about  some easter eggs that were sprinkled  throughout the series for starters in  uncharted 1 the wetsuits that nate and  elena are wearing are from a brand named  otzel this just so happens to be the  same name as daxter's species in jack  and daxter another game from naughty dog  half otter half weasel full auto in fact  a picture of daxter can be seen on the  sleeve of the wetsuit just in case you  needed a little more proof but that's  not the only time naughty dog makes a  reference to their pre-uncharted  releases sully's plane the wild hog is  actually a reference to a leveling crash  bandicoot that shares the same name it's  a level that many fans consider to be  very frustrating over in uncharted 3  naughty dog did the opposite and made a  reference to one of their upcoming games  instead following the fight in the  opening of the game if you head to the  corner of the bar instead of following  sully there is a newspaper that says  scientists are still struggling to  understand deadly fungus this paper was  reportedly meant to be taken out  pre-released as not to spoil the last of  us reveal a month later but clearly it  wasn't a big deal now if the headline  read something like our next game is a  zombie survival game then that might  have been actually worth scrapping the  last of us has some references to  uncharted as well however you'll have to  wait for a things you didn't know about  the last of us video also in uncharted 3  there is a little shout out to a  non-naughty dog game in the form of  little big planet sacboy a key chain of  the character can be seen hanging in the  front of a bus that nate and the gang  make an escape in and that reminds me  have you ever noticed that nate always  manages to make an escape the man is  very lucky so lucky that naughty dog  shows you when he's starting to run out  of luck on screen according to naughty  dog animator jonathan cooper all bullets  flying nate's way are near misses not  hits the player's screen turning red  indicates nate's luck running out he  doesn't actually take bullet damage  until he becomes an unlucky duck and the  enemy gets that one clear shot this is  by far my least favorite uncharted fact  and i laugh every time i think about it  but i think the reason it seems so  strange to me is because so many other  games have gotten me used to the idea  that red screen equals lowered health  from taking damage i can't hate on  naughty dog for trying to be a little  different another fact that you may not  have known is that sam nate's brother  was originally a villain of sorts in  uncharted 4. during an interview amy  hennig the game's former director and  writer explained that the drake brothers  had a different relationship in the  original script hennig said quote i mean  i wouldn't call him the antagonist in  the classic sense but it was an  antagonistic force in drake's life that  he had to reconcile so it was you know  complicated by stuff coming up from the  past so it's a little different than him  showing up and you know hey bro i got a  problem i'm in a lot of trouble here  what  i'm talking about what kind of trouble  hennig also reveals that nadine wasn't  in her original story at all so remember  kids anything is possible nadine went  from not existing to getting her own  spin-off with chloe but did you know  that those adventurous women weren't  naughty dog's first choice sam and sully  were actually first up for the game but  the idea was tossed because of sully's  age at the time uncharted 4 takes place  next in line for consideration was  cassie but the idea was scrapped because  the devs didn't love the idea of a  teenager mass murdering goons thus the  lost legacy we know and love was born  you have a plan  sure  before we close out here's a bonus fact  about nate  his greatest fear  is clowns according to nate those  red-nosed humans are a 10 out of 10 on  his fear scale i've never quite  understood the fear of clowns but my  fear of bugs are like a 9 out of 10 on  my fear of scales so i i'll respect it  and leave clowns out of my uncharted fan  fiction  but alright thanks for watching hit the  like button if you've enjoyed this video  at all and then hit the comment section  and let us know if we missed any facts  see in the next one  [Music]  you
 

